"plan.rounds" = "Focus sessions per set: %d";
"plan.rounds_help" = "A full focus session counts once. The last session in a set is followed by a long break. Postponing or skipping a break never adds another session.";
"plan.actions_help" = "Postponing keeps this break and restarts its full duration when the reminder returns, up to the configured limit. Skip ends this break and returns to work, keeping actual rest time without counting a completed break. In round-based plans, skipping a mid-focus break resumes the remaining focus time; skipping a break after focus ends starts the next round, or a new group after the final round.";
"plan.away_help" = "When time away is detected, a long enough absence can satisfy a break. In the dual-interval model, a short absence resets only the short timer; a long one resets both. Locking or sleeping also pauses timing.";
"plan.rounds_away" = "Time away never completes a focus session. If you step away for at least the short break duration, the current focus session restarts and earlier sessions are kept. An absence as long as a long break starts a new set. During a due break, time away can satisfy that break.";
"plan.switch_help" = "Applying a plan starts a new timing cycle. During a break, the plan takes effect when the break completes or is skipped. A paused timer stays paused. Other preferences and history are preserved.";
